Subject: [PATCH] BluetoothDevice: add MediaTek getLinkKeyPersistState()

MtkBt.apk's OPP receive dialog calls it to decide whether to offer
"remember my choice"; without it the dialog crashes with
NoSuchMethodError. Derived from the bond state: BlueAngel drops
non-persistent link keys together with the bond.

---
diff --git a/core/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothDevice.java b/core/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothDevice.java
index 8df7647154d..787a7731800 100644
--- a/core/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothDevice.java
+++ b/core/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothDevice.java
@@ -745,6 +745,23 @@ public final class BluetoothDevice implements Parcelable {
         return BOND_NONE;
     }
 
+    /** @hide */
+    public static final int LINK_KEY_NOT_EXIST = -1;
+    /** @hide */
+    public static final int LINK_KEY_PERSIST_YES = 0;
+    /** @hide */
+    public static final int LINK_KEY_PERSIST_NO = 1;
+
+    /**
+     * MediaTek API used by MtkBt.apk: whether the link key to this device
+     * is stored. BlueAngel drops non-persistent keys on disconnect, which
+     * also removes the bond, so a bonded device has a persistent key.
+     * @hide
+     */
+    public int getLinkKeyPersistState() {
+        return getBondState() == BOND_BONDED ? LINK_KEY_PERSIST_YES : LINK_KEY_NOT_EXIST;
+    }
+
     /**
      * Get the Bluetooth class of the remote device.
      * <p>Requires {@link android.Manifest.permission#BLUETOOTH}.
